<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-136] zeppelin delete paragraph content after &quot;Move up&quot; operation if paragraph did not run before</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-136</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When using the move up option on a paragraph which was run before zeppelin delete the paragraph content. &lt;br/&gt;
ALSO, after move up, new paragraph can&apos;t be added to the notebook at the end.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Step to repro:&lt;br/&gt;
Open new notebook&lt;br/&gt;
add some test in paragraph 1 using %md and execute it&lt;br/&gt;
add some text in paragraph two but DO NOT execute it&lt;br/&gt;
using the right gear, click on move up&lt;br/&gt;
the paragraph is deleted&lt;br/&gt;
also, no way to add new paragraph at the end of the notebook.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;corneadoug@apache.org comments on this one:&lt;br/&gt;
So I guess what is happening is that when you do a &apos;move up&apos;, it sends the&lt;br/&gt;
action to websocket for save (only the move up action).&lt;br/&gt;
And websocket send you the notebook as result (based on the notebook file),&lt;br/&gt;
which is then replacing the one in your view.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
